      "category": "transmission",
      "title": "4L60E Automatic Transmission Failure",
      "description": "The 4L60E transmission is known for 3-4 clutch pack burnup, sun shell failure, and worn input drum. These trucks were often used for towing which accelerated wear. The transmission develops slipping in 3rd and 4th gears.",
      "solution": "Confirm the failure with a road test and scan for transmission codes, then check fluid condition and line pressure; burnt fluid, slipping in 3rd/4th, or a flare on the 2-3 shift usually points to a failed 3-4 clutch pack, worn input drum, or a damaged sun shell. The proper repair is removal and rebuild or replacement of the 4L60E, typically including an upgraded 3-4 clutch pack, reinforced sun shell (“Beast” style), input drum/hardened shell components, new seals and bushings, and inspection or replacement of the torque converter; the cooler and lines must also be flushed or replaced to prevent repeat failure. If valve body wear or shift solenoid issues are found, install a valve body repair kit or replace the affected solenoids during overhaul. Typical cost is about $2,000-$3,500 for a quality rebuild/remanufactured unit installed, with higher cost possible if hard parts are heavily damaged.",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "symptoms": [
        "Slipping in 3rd or 4th gear",
        "Harsh 1-2 shift",
        "No 3rd or 4th gear",
        "Burnt fluid smell"
      ],
